  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M.V.Paul vs Union Of India on 15 January, 2024 Author: Amit Rawal Bench: Amit Rawal In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable Mr. Justice Amit Rawal Monday, The 15Th Day Of January 2024 / 25Th Pousha, 1945 Wp(C) No. 38700 Of 2015 Petitioner: M.V.Paul S/O.Vareeth, Mambrakkaran House, Perembra, Kodakara, Trichur 680689 By Advs. Sri.Santhosh Subramanian Sri.Sherry J. Thomas Sri.S.Sreekumarnorth Paravur Sri.E.A.Thankappan Respondents: 1 Union Of India Represented By Secretary Ministry Of Health & Family Welfare, New Delhi 110 107. 2 Food Safety And Standards Authority Of India New Delhi, Represented By Its Member/Secretary, Fssai, New Delhi 110 107. 3 State Of Kerala Represented By Its Chief Secretary, Government Secretariat Thiruvananthapuram 695001. 4 Commissioner Of Food Safety For The State Of Kerala Thiruvananthapuram 695014. 5 ASSISTANT COMMISSIONER OF FOOD SAFETY (DESIGNATED OFFICER) M.G.ROAD, TRICHUR 680 001. 6 FOOD SAFETY OFFICER CHALAKKUDY CIRCLE, CHALAKKUDY P.O., TRICHUR 680 307. BY ADV SRI.JAGADEESH LAKSHMAN, CGC THIS WRIT PETITION (CIVIL) HAVING COME UP FOR HEARING ON 15.01.2024, THE COURT ON THE SAME DAY DELIVERED THE FOLLOWING: M.V.Paul vs Union Of India on 15 January, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/171795231/ 1 WP(C) NO. 38700 OF 2015 2 JUDGMENT Order Ext.P3 is concededly appealable under Section 46(4) of the then Food and Safety Standards Act, 2006 and the rules and regulations made thereunder.",
